{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/444893-combating-the-strix","id":444893,"title":"Combating the Strix","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-16T14:28:50-07:00","id":444893,"title":"Combating the Strix","content":"I've been running a game for a while now in which the Strix have been a background danger to the city, and the PCs have now decided to take action.<br /> <br /> Luckily for them, one of their number is a Kaibit (as per <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp/</a>), which makes identifying the Strix easy enough. So now they know that there are two Strix active in the city, one posessing a human, a corrupt, abusive cop, and the other possessing a well-liked Carthian agitator who is suddenly arguing far more aggressive and rigourous rebellion.<br /> Having ID'd these two, but having trouble convincing other a lot of others, they are asking around about the best ways to trap, expel or destroy a Strix, and they have managed to get occult scholars from both the Ordo Dracul &amp; Lancea et Sanctum to at least entertain the notion for a mental exercise or similar.<br /> Given some time, and some half-decent expertise, what ideas could a local kindred occult scholar come up with, short of killing the host in broad daylight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3580-monkeybloke","name":"MonkeyBloke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T14:56:40-07:00","id":444931,"title":"","content":"The easiest way to kill a Strix inside a host would be to use fire. Fire will still damage a host as normal, and if the host perishes while being surrounded by flames, the Strix will be expelled directly into one of their banes, be unable to move, and start taking damage. If you can get away with it, light a known host's haven on fire.<br /> <br /> Failing that, blood magic can be used to hurt the Strix, as can the updated Khaibit powers. Khaibit make excellent Strix hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2984-jibkisamabi","name":"JibKisamabi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T15:23:43-07:00","id":444978,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Fire, sorcery, and the unique powers of the Khaibit are all capable of harming the Strix in their native shadow form, which is the real trick of Strix-hunting. Anybody can destroy their host bodies, but if you don't want them coming back again, you need something that can affect noncorporeal entities. Or just kill them with fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T17:10:57-07:00","id":445090,"title":"","content":"The solution I brought up in <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?734837-Vampire-The-Requiem-2nd-Edition-Nobody-Wants-You\" target=\"_blank\">the Strix-centric chronicle</a> I ran last year was to gather intelligence on previous attacks, which pointed to common Strix banes and the possibility of obscure ones.<br /> <br /> The PCs reached out to mortal and Kindred occult groups, tried a few ideas, and found one that sounded promising. (This in turn involved potentially overturning the Kindred society of a major city by reviving a tyrannical elder kept in torpor for over a century, but eggs and omelettes.)<br /> <br /> I gave this particular Strix &quot;family&quot; a magical bane that could be recreated by a ritual known only to the elder, which gave the group a weapon against them that they couldn't mass produce, and they would have to take out the Strix &quot;elder&quot; to stop the incursion.<br /> <br /> Another advantage which came up in passing is that as of second edition, vampires can function in daylight for at least a while, and the Strix can't. This let the PCs escape an ambush and keep fleeing until sunrise, then rest up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T23:46:06-07:00","id":445414,"title":"","content":"Make friends with a Bone Shadow.<br /> Suggest that you have a <u><i><b>GREAT</b></i></u> target for Siskur-Dah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T06:39:38-07:00","id":445736,"title":"","content":"Or a Storm Lord, since the Strix are akin to Claimed when they have a host.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T08:09:21-07:00","id":445892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/444893-combating-the-strix?p=445414#post445414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make friends with a Bone Shadow.<br /> Suggest that you have a <u><i><b>GREAT</b></i></u> target for Siskur-Dah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strix aren't ephemeral entities though. ._.<br /> <br /> Part of what makes them so hard to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T08:26:40-07:00","id":445956,"title":"","content":"True, but they can turn into twilight, at wich point the Bone Shadow can proceed to mess it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:03:02-07:00","id":446016,"title":"","content":"That frequency thing becomes a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:11:26-07:00","id":446020,"title":"","content":"Would frequency be an issue? They're not ephemera, so they don't seem to work off that frequency thing, otherwise they wouldn't be calling them Tengu in Tokyo.<br /> <br /> Depending on how literal you take the line 'Strix are creatures of death and impending doom,' you may be able to use Barghest to deal with them in Twilight, as it attunes the user to fight ghosts and undead or death-infused beings. The Twilight Purge rite kicks things out of Twilight, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:27:06-07:00","id":446043,"title":"","content":"The problem with that rite and similar ones is that it might be <i>easier</i> to hurt them if they're in Twilight or in the Shadow. In the physical world, they are very much like shadows. You can't grab shadows or hurt them.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">Except with Fire. And some Werewolves will have Influence: Fire, conveniently enough.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:32:14-07:00","id":446047,"title":"","content":"Even without the elemental gifts you can have fetishes that grant Influence: Fire or even Influence: Sunlight. Plus there's at least one gift that finds the banes of spirits, and it would take a fetish to translate that to finding the banes of other things, which could include strix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T13:10:13-07:00","id":446418,"title":"","content":"Which makes an interesting story, because a werewolf is gonna expect you to help him back. It might be worth the trade off, but you're just one (or more) leeches in a new, scary world. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T13:37:28-07:00","id":446487,"title":"","content":"Only some of the most powerful strix have the ability to take a twilight form. In that form they would be vulnerable to a werewolf since the purpose is for the strix to get on the same &quot;frequency&quot; to feed on ghosts and spirits, at least they would be as vulnerable as a spirit in twilight. It was made pretty clear that a power needs to have control of shadows to be able to hurt a strix. There might be some werewolf power out there like that. A mage would have an easier time. The problem is the strix could possess them too, as possess living. A strix can possess any supernatural, so unless you like the idea of killing your helper and any chance they had of helping you kill the strix, not the best idea you could come up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T16:05:47-07:00","id":446655,"title":"","content":"I think it was Gift or Rite, that lets you interact with any twilight entity, spirits, ghosts, you name it. A werewolf may very well be unnable to see them, but can harm them if they manage to overcome that limitation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T16:17:25-07:00","id":446668,"title":"","content":"So, werewolves &amp; mages aside, fire is the most obvious weapon, although the host is toast.<br /> Here is something that came up tonight - can a kindred use Domiate on a Strix? (I don't see why not, it has resistance and Shadow Potency).<br /> Do you dominate the Strix or the host? (I'd assume the Strix).<br /> Can you dominate a Strix to leave the host? (Any reason why not?).<br /> As it stands, with a PC Khaibit &amp; a PC Ventrue who specialises in Dominate, is there any reason they can't spot &amp; dominate the Strix?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3580-monkeybloke","name":"MonkeyBloke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T18:11:20-07:00","id":446828,"title":"","content":"Going off memory and what I've checked, no there isn't anything stopping a vampire from Dominating a Strix. So in theory yes, you could Dominate the Strix into leaving the host. Once they're out of the host however, you would then need to destroy the Strix before it escaped, or risk it simply finding another host to start the dance all over again. Khaibit powers would come in handy there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2984-jibkisamabi","name":"JibKisamabi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T18:30:09-07:00","id":446838,"title":"","content":"There's a Dread Power they can take which they can use which has some nasty effects on those that try to Majesty or Dominate them. Not all Strix will have it, but it was said to be very common during the Fall of the Camarilla, for instance. So that's something to keep in mind as a player, they might hear stories of how the Strix could turn it back on their would-be lords and seducers, and realize they should take care not to try it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T19:04:54-07:00","id":446886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/444893-combating-the-strix?p=446655#post446655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it was Gift or Rite, that lets you interact with any twilight entity, spirits, ghosts, you name it. A werewolf may very well be unnable to see them, but can harm them if they manage to overcome that limitation.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't an issue of sight. Everyone can see a strix normally. Most strix can't enter into twilight. Strix are not naturally twilight entities so you would be using something to force them into twilight then something else to affect twilight entities. Strix aren't made of ephemera. They are made of very real shadows which makes them untouchable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T19:19:52-07:00","id":446898,"title":"","content":"It would definitely be the strix that would get dominated. They certainly can get dominated, see Indomitable p. 211 VtR 2.0. They wouldn't have a power to make them immune if they were already. Dominate 5 is likely out, but telling the strix to leave the host should be fine unless it was obviously suicidal or synthesis prevented it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T04:34:44-07:00","id":447486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/444893-combating-the-strix?p=446886#post446886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't an issue of sight. Everyone can see a strix normally. Most strix can't enter into twilight. Strix are not naturally twilight entities so you would be using something to force them into twilight then something else to affect twilight entities. Strix aren't made of ephemera. They are made of very real shadows which makes them untouchable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, I meant <i>if</i> the Strix turns into twilight form, they would be on a diferent frequency from that that werewolves can normally see (the spirit's one), but the power to afect them is a blank afects anything in twilight, so there's the conundrum of being able to hit something that you cannot percieve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T07:25:38-07:00","id":447664,"title":"","content":"Actually twilight strix seem to squat over all frequencies. they can affect spirits physically, which implies they can be seen by anything that can see spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T08:58:19-07:00","id":447748,"title":"","content":"Yes they don't seem to be on a frequency, that seems to be an ephemeral thing, and strix aren't ephemerals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T13:49:43-07:00","id":448208,"title":"","content":"Gotcha. I think they then are on the spirit and ghost frequencies when they take a twilight form. A werewolf should be able to see them as well as a spirit then. Not the best path for a strix since they would have gained two tribes as enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T14:08:45-07:00","id":448244,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking of giving all local strix a running water bane whether embodied or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T06:31:14-07:00","id":449111,"title":"","content":"The Lancea Sanctum. Seriously. They DO have exorcism rituals. Pull that creature out of the body, then trap it in fire, let the sunlight hit it in a few hours. Or trick it into a corpse after the exorcism, and then light that up.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you allow Cruac to have exorcism powers, or non-mortals to perform exorcisms, all the better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T18:58:18-07:00","id":450013,"title":"","content":"Ever since Hurt Locker playtest notes, I've wanted to play a Khaibit with an Owl and Falconry... Pseshkf an Owl... Using an Owl to fight strix seems epic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T20:12:06-07:00","id":451233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/444893-combating-the-strix?p=449111#post449111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lancea Sanctum. Seriously. They DO have exorcism rituals. Pull that creature out of the body, then trap it in fire, let the sunlight hit it in a few hours. Or trick it into a corpse after the exorcism, and then light that up.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you allow Cruac to have exorcism powers, or non-mortals to perform exorcisms, all the better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought exorcism and abjuration didn't work on strix?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T22:26:08-07:00","id":451305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/444893-combating-the-strix?p=451233#post451233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought exorcism and abjuration didn't work on strix?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's one of the Banes they can potentially acquire as they get older, so #notallstrix","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T09:18:14-07:00","id":451604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/444893-combating-the-strix?p=451233#post451233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought exorcism and abjuration didn't work on strix?</div> </div> </div> </div> Leet hit general, but specifically on the topic of Theban / Cruac... <br /> <br /> Requiem for Rome had specific rituals meant to deal with casting out strix possessing bodies, both for Theban, and Veneficia (which basically uses same rituals as Cruac). Even if your ST doesn't keep those specific rituals, it makes sense for the magics to have something.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T06:54:40-07:00","id":458033,"title":"","content":"If you are using Sacraments and Blasphemies for your blood sorcery, then it's pretty easy to ramp various blood sorceries up to dealing Agg damage, or augmenting attacks to deal Agg damage, which the Strix are explicitly vulnerable to in any form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T07:14:31-07:00","id":458037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/444893-combating-the-strix?p=458033#post458033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are using Sacraments and Blasphemies for your blood sorcery, then it's pretty easy to ramp various blood sorceries up to dealing Agg damage, or augmenting attacks to deal Agg damage, which the Strix are explicitly vulnerable to in any form.</div> </div> </div> </div>By pretty easy, he means that you need Blood Sorcery at 5, with very specific Themes chosen (that is Destruction). <br /> <br /> Not that easy, depending on how hard it is to learn disciplines in the specific game and on how common is Destruction theme <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T07:57:32-07:00","id":458060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/444893-combating-the-strix?p=458037#post458037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By pretty easy, he means that you need Blood Sorcery at 5, with very specific Themes chosen (that is Destruction).<br /> <br /> Not that easy, depending on how hard it is to learn disciplines in the specific game and on how common is Destruction theme <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you actually only need Destruction 4 to upgrade Lethal base attacks to Agg. Creation 3 allows for the potential manipulations of thunderstorms... though I don't know whether or not lightning counts as fire for the purposes of banes. Transmutation 3 could arguably change a strix into a corporeal form, and inarguably do so by the 5th dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3081,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","user":"Anachronistic Jam","date":". 03-26-2015, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T10:45:43-07:00","id":458151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/444893-combating-the-strix?p=446418#post446418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which makes an interesting story, because a werewolf is gonna expect you to help him back. It might be worth the trade off, but you're just one (or more) leeches in a new, scary world. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Depends.<br /> <br /> nWoD doesn't have the back end metaplot reasoning for Uratha to lash out against Kindred. Both are wary of each other because let's face it, both cultures are based on a secret society of which the slightest mistake or slip of the tongue can result in your death.<br /> <br /> But outright hate? Not very much. Aside from maybe the Uratha beating the crap out of the Ordo and the Crone but that's out of Kindred fucking with the Shadow, less so that the Uratha feel the need to kill all Kindred on site.<br /> <br /> I can see mutual backscratching from the Invictus, the Movement, and, oddly enough, the Lance on material issues (Uratha pack wants to improve it's territory, Kindred needs the Strix to stay the fuck away.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T10:57:09-07:00","id":458154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/444893-combating-the-strix?p=458151#post458151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But outright hate? Not very much. Aside from maybe the Uratha beating the crap out of the Ordo and the Crone but that's out of Kindred fucking with the Shadow, less so that the Uratha feel the need to kill all Kindred on site.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do the Crone fuck with the shadow? I was under the impression that was outside the purview of most blood magic.<br /> <br /> As for dislike, I actually think that werewolves would almost categorically dislike vampires, as their existence feeds all sorts of negative memes shadow-side. You get your typical coterie in your territory and it's likely to become a quickly losing battle against spirits of excess, fear, and death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T11:22:32-07:00","id":458165,"title":"","content":"Officially speaking, I don't think that vampiric blood magic can deliberately mess with the Shadow in any meaningful way, though it might theoretically cause some kind of spiritual side-effect that vampires don't notice. The Circle and the L+S probably don't know much more about the Shadow than mortal occultists do, though the life span of those groups and their members mean that they probably have more data to work with than almost anyone else confined to the physical world. <br /> <br /> Frankly, anybody with blood has a decent reason not to like vampires by default. Werewolf packs tend to be very family-oriented, and in many cases have a fairly broad definition of family. If the local werewolves find out that some vampire has added one of the wolf-blooded to their herd, that's likely to put the leech on their shit list pretty quick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T12:55:31-07:00","id":458284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/444893-combating-the-strix?p=458154#post458154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do the Crone fuck with the shadow? I was under the impression that was outside the purview of most blood magic.<br /> <br /> As for dislike, I actually think that werewolves would almost categorically dislike vampires, as their existence feeds all sorts of negative memes shadow-side. You get your typical coterie in your territory and it's likely to become a quickly losing battle against spirits of excess, fear, and death.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Crone book, there are optional Cruac rituals in which the Acolytes misunderstand the purpose of the ritual and how it interacts with spirits. In short, Kindred having access in areas they don't quite understand.<br /> <br /> Again. Most Kindred are not the Brood or to use oWod terms, The Sabbat and Kindred have the social levers which can greatly enhance territory. Pack been dealing with territory with junkies and high unemployment? City suddenly has a new &quot;job initiative&quot; focused on building industry in the territory. Pack dealing with a nearby locus being threaten by city action? Boom, historical landmark.<br /> <br /> Dislike and being wary of is one thing but even there is mutual understanding of &quot;what can you do for me?&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T13:50:21-07:00","id":458326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/444893-combating-the-strix?p=458284#post458284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dislike and being wary of is one thing but even there is mutual understanding of &quot;what can you do for me?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's not entirely what Anachronistic Jam is talking about, is it? If you've got a vampire in your turf, that means that the spirits of fear, blood, death, etc are getting fed and at the same time your loved ones are at risk. So if you can hunt down and kill a spirit/something else which endangers them, why not vampires? I do believe in not having default aggravated relationships between the splats, but let's face it. Vampires will get on the bad side of werewolves more often than not, just because of their nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T14:30:37-07:00","id":458349,"title":"","content":"Well, I mean, that sounds like a solid half of the <i>raison d'etre </i>of the Iron Masters, so it seems working as intended to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T14:31:34-07:00","id":458350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/444893-combating-the-strix?p=458326#post458326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that's not entirely what Anachronistic Jam is talking about, is it? If you've got a vampire in your turf, that means that the spirits of fear, blood, death, etc are getting fed and at the same time your loved ones are at risk. So if you can hunt down and kill a spirit/something else which endangers them, why not vampires? I do believe in not having default aggravated relationships between the splats, but let's face it. Vampires will get on the bad side of werewolves more often than not, just because of their nature.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not all werewolves operate in the same territory as their family. And not all vampires operate by spreading fear and death. Certainly some do but others can be more subtle. Since this spawned off of a talk about Cruac, the sorcery resonates with themes of creation and protection. While the sorcery could be used for evil deeds, it's not fair to say all Cruac is going to create nasty spirits that need to be destroyed.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, keep in mind that werewolves aren't about protecting people, they're about protecting the two worlds by keeping them apart. While some packs may decide to take a more heroic, defender of mankind point of view, others may only care about the strength of the Gauntlet in their territory. And of course, since vampires can now be part of a werewolf's pack, they can just as easily make an arrangement. Rather than give birth to spirits of war and hate and murder by killing them and their ghouls, you could just let them know who is off limits to them and work from there.<br /> <br /> Of course some werewolves, like Black Moon eXtreme and the Eaters of the Dead are just straight out vampire hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T17:22:43-07:00","id":460524,"title":"","content":"Let's say a Khaibit made a ghoul, what parts of Obtenebration couldn't a ghoul learn? Also is Obtenebration still learnable by non-Khaibit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}